{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012XPBotPWyCAZBDNnyqQEL4","type":"tool_result","content":"42:if (E.targets(guard, [hero], { range: 60 }).length) throw new Error('not on the same level: no melee target');\n166:- `E.inArc(a, facing, b, range, halfAngle, dz)`: melee cone on the ground: is b (with optional radius r) within range of a and within halfAngle of facing? dz (optional) also limits the height difference, so a hero on a roof can't hit a guard in the street (left out, height is ignored)\n187:- `E.targets(from, list, o = {})`: the things in list that `from` can reach, nearest first, each as { target, d (ground distance), dz, angle (from -> it) }: melee auto-aim, lock-on, takedowns, interaction prompts. o: { range, arc (half angle around facing, radians; default all round), facing (de\n261:- `game.screen.filter = 'clean'` †: 'clean' | 'scanlines' | 'crt', drawn over the picture as it is presented, never on the buffer, and not under a test harness (navigator.webdriver). game.settings.filter sets it\n266:- `game.screen.scale = 'auto'`: how a fixed resolution fills the screen: 'sharp' (whole-number scale, every pixel the same size, black bars unless o.expand grows the picture into them), 'fill' (the largest fit, pixels a device pixel apart in size) or 'auto' (fill on high-density screens, phones \n278:- `input.bindings` †: the player's bindings over the preset: { action: { keys: [codes], pad: [codes] } } (game.settings.bindings keeps them)\n341:- `input.rumbleScale = .6` †: vibration strength 0..1 (0 = off; game.settings.rumble sets it)\n431:- `r.sightCone(obs, o = {})` †: an observer's view on the ground: a dithered fan fov wide (radians) about its facing, out to range, cut short where the map hides a body's chest (map.ray, the height rules), draped over the ground below. o: { range: 120, fov: 1.6, facing, map, eye, color: '#ffe080\n468:- `game.addPlayer(o = {})` †: a player in now: { pad: index } (a gamepad) or { keys: 'right' } (the keyboard's right half; player 1 takes the left). Returns its input (null when four play already)\n478:- `game.flash(color = '#ffffff', seconds = .12, strength = 1)`: flash the whole screen with a color for `seconds` (dithered fade out): hits, explosions, lightning. Shorter when reduceMotion, dimmer by the player's settings.flashes\n484:- `game.menu(name)`: open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without scenes) pauses on its pause screen; any other scene, a title, waits under the settings. menu('settings') or menu('controls') opens that screen. Without a menu (men\n492:- `game.resetCamera()` †: undo setZoom and rotateView: the scene's own zoom again (camera.start, or camera.tall on a screen held upright; 1 without), no turn. The player's zoom stays (settings.zoom)\n499:- `game.shake(a)`: shake the screen by a (pixels, decaying; at most 10 in all); none when reduceMotion, scaled by the player's settings.shake\n505:- `game.start({ camera })`: a scene's { zoom: [.75, 2], start: 1, tall: 1.5, wheel: true }: the player zooms the camera within zoom (the wheel, - and =, a pinch, Settings, Camera zoom: theirs, kept, on top of the game's; false or none: they can't; a function of the game: a range per screen shape\n511:- `game.zoomBy(k)` †: the player zooms the camera by a factor (1.1: 10% closer, .9: farther), as the wheel, - and = and a pinch do (a zoom button of the game's own can): within the scene's camera.zoom range, kept as their setting (settings.zoom, on top of the game's zoom), and noted at the top o\n512:- `game.zoomRange()` †: the zooms the player may take the camera to here, [min, max] (the scene's camera.zoom, or the game's; a function of the game gives one per screen shape or level), or null where they can't (camera.zoom false or none)\n518:- `game.cam`: camera. smooth = seconds of lag; bounds(view) = clamp rect; room = [w, h] world units for screen-by-screen rooms; moving = sliding between rooms; offset = [dx, dy] screen pixels from the screen's centre to where the focus sits (above a phone's touch buttons: [0, -40]); x, y: the ca\n521:- `game.drawEvery = 1`: 1, or 2 while a fast display (a 120 Hz phone) refreshes quicker than the game can draw (a frame's cost, or refreshes missed: its GPU behind): every other refresh is drawn, evenly, instead of random ones missed (the updates still run every refresh). The player's Frame rate\n544:- `game.settings`: the player's choices (game.settings.volume, game.settings.set('volume', .5), your own from menu.settings), saved and applied (section 10b)\n558:- `game.zoom = 1` †: the camera's zoom now (1 = as the view is): the game's (setZoom, a scene's camera.start) times the player's (settings.zoom: the wheel, a pinch), within the scene's camera.zoom range\n564:- `settings.default(key)`: a setting's default value\n565:- `settings.define(sp)`: add a setting: { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', value, min, max, step, options: [[value, label]] or [value], help, group: 'Game', apply(game, value) }. Its saved value is loaded (when it is a valid one) and applied; it shows on the settings screen. Ret\n566:- `settings.keys(group)`: the keys of a group's settings, in order ('Display', 'Sound', 'Comfort', 'Controller', 'Touch', 'Game'), or every key\n567:- `settings.reset(group)`: put a group's settings (or all of them) back to their defaults; a game's saves are not touched\n568:- `settings.set(key, v)`: change a setting: checked (a slider kept in range, a choice among its options), saved, applied, onChange told. Returns the value kept (the old one when v is not a valid value)\n569:- `settings.spec(key)`: the spec a setting was defined with (its label, type, range, options), or undefined\n570:- `settings.saved`: false when the last save failed (storage blocked or full: the choices last for this visit)\n576:- `fullscreen.toggle()`: full screen on or off, as the player asked (the corner's button, the menu): their choice is kept in settings.fullscreen, so a game starting on a phone goes full screen by itself only while they haven't turned it off\n1015:- `E.sees(obs, tgt, o = {})`: can observer see target? { seen, d (ground distance), angle (observer -> target), exposure: 0..1 }. The target must be within range and inside the cone fov wide (radians) about the observer's facing; exposure is the share of three points on it (its feet, its chest,\n1053:- `game.audio.calibrate()` †: the audio offset's calibration: a click on each beat (100 bpm, the first of a bar higher) as the music; tap(time) on each one heard (an event's timeStamp, or nothing: this update step). After 8 taps, result is the offset to set (ms: settings.audioOffset) and done i\n1074:- `game.audio.offset = 0` †: seconds the music sounds early, for speakers and headphones that lag (settings.audioOffset)\n1166:- `new E.Shell({ settings })`: settings.items: the game's own settings, { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', min, max, step, options, value } (kept in game.settings, beside the standard ones)\n1176:- `shell.hud({ prompt })` †: { key: 'E' (or act: 'interact': its key on the player's device), label, hint, progress: 0..1 }\n1177:- `shell.hud({ keys, buttons })` †: keys: [['WASD', 'Move'], ...] (hidden on touch screens); buttons: [[label, fn or action]] (top right: pause and map where there is no Escape key)\n1180:- `shell.settings` †: the player's settings: game.settings (the standard ones and the game's own, by key)\n1183:- `shell.show('help')` †: { keys: [[key, what]], sections: [[heading, text]] }\n1311:- `car.charge = 0`: a kart's drift boost building (1 blue, 2 orange)\n1364:- `new E.Fighter(game, o = {}) → fighter` †: new E.Fighter(game, { name, x, side: 1 (faces right), rig: Humanoid options (or a Humanoid), life: 1000, walk: 75, back: 60, jump: 390, jumpX: 90, moves, throwBtn: 'hp', throwRange, throwDmg: 120, input })\n1458:- `grid.threat(units, o = {})`: what a side can strike on its next turn: units ([{ cx, cy, move, range: [min, max] or n (1), climb, drop }]) each moving within its reach (o.blocked: cells it can't enter) and striking within range of where it stops. { cells: [[cx, cy, n]], count(c), by(c) -> [un\n1487:- `E.tint(r, cells, color, alpha = .4, T = 16, height = null)`: tints on cells' tops: E.tint(r, cells ([[cx, cy], ...]), color, alpha = .4, T = 16, height(cx, cy) = 0): a move range, a path, an attack's reach, drawn on the floor (decals) where height is 0; on a raised top (a TileMap wall's) it\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174825__x17a627/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"10fd43c2-a819-4540-9aa0-cc285e3b03f8","uuid":"d7330e53-d765-4f65-b895-0e58036b0f46","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:53:38.998Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"42:if (E.targets(guard, [hero], { range: 60 }).length) throw new Error('not on the same level: no melee target');\n166:- `E.inArc(a, facing, b, range, halfAngle, dz)`: melee cone on the ground: is b (with optional radius r) within range of a and within halfAngle of facing? dz (optional) also limits the height difference, so a hero on a roof can't hit a guard in the street (left out, height is ignored)\n187:- `E.targets(from, list, o = {})`: the things in list that `from` can reach, nearest first, each as { target, d (ground distance), dz, angle (from -> it) }: melee auto-aim, lock-on, takedowns, interaction prompts. o: { range, arc (half angle around facing, radians; default all round), facing (de\n261:- `game.screen.filter = 'clean'` †: 'clean' | 'scanlines' | 'crt', drawn over the picture as it is presented, never on the buffer, and not under a test harness (navigator.webdriver). game.settings.filter sets it\n266:- `game.screen.scale = 'auto'`: how a fixed resolution fills the screen: 'sharp' (whole-number scale, every pixel the same size, black bars unless o.expand grows the picture into them), 'fill' (the largest fit, pixel