{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0149Fn6tve4FmNJuHbajSPps","type":"tool_result","content":"1120\t| yorker | pace | 136–146 | 0.15 | 0.5 | 0 | 0.9 | 0.1 | length band 0–24 from the crease |\n1121\t| slower | pace | 105–115 | 0 | 1.2 | 0 | 0.95 | 0.3 | looks like an express until late (no speed shown until it pitches) |\n1122\t| outswing | swing | 125–135 | +1.0 | 1.0 | 0 | 1.0 | 0 | |\n1123\t| inswing | swing | 125–135 | −1.0 | 1.0 | 0 | 1.0 | 0 | |\n1124\t| wobble | swing | 120–130 | ±0.3 random | 3.0 | 0 | 1.0 | 0 | |\n1125\t| dobber | medium | 100–110 | 0.1 | 1.5 | 0 | 0.95 | 0.1 | |\n1126\t| cutter | medium | 105–115 | 0 | 1.0 | +3 | 0.95 | 0 | |\n1127\t| knuckle | medium | 95–105 | wobbly flight | 0.5 | 0 | 0.9 | 0.25 | |\n1128\t| legbreak | spin | 78–88 | drift −0.3 | 0.3 | +9 | 1.05 | 0.2 | |\n1129\t| googly | spin | 76–86 | drift +0.2 | 0.3 | −8 | 1.05 | 0.2 | |\n1130\t| topspin | spin | 80–90 | 0 | 0.3 | 0 | 1.2 | 0.35 | |\n1131\t| offbreak | spin | 80–90 | drift +0.3 | 0.3 | −8 | 1.0 | 0.15 | |\n1132\t| armball | spin | 88–96 | +0.3 | 0.3 | 0 | 0.95 | 0 | |\n1133\t| doosra | spin | 78–88 | 0 | 0.3 | +8 | 1.05 | 0.2 | |\n1134\t| piston | machine | 160–170 | 0 | 0.8 | 0 | 1.05 | 0 | the Thrumptonator only |\n1135\t| steamBouncer | machine | 150 | 0 | 1.0 | 0 | 1.35 | 0 | steam trail |\n1136\t| spinCycle | machine | 95 | 0 | 0 | ±14 random | 1.1 | 0.3 | |\n1137\t\n1138\tSwing base acceleration: 60 u/s² × swing × `T('swing')` × ground factor. Each bowler lists 3 deliveries from their family (plus a special).\n1139\t\n1140\t#### 8.4.2 Field presets (θ° from straight, + = off side; distance in units; the keeper is extra)\n1141\t- **Attacking pace:** slip1 165/150, slip2 158/150, slip3 151/152, gully 132/150, point 95/230, cover 58/260, mid-off 14/300, mid-on −14/300, fine leg −162/(boundary − 30).\n1142\t- **Balanced:** slip1 165/150, point 95/240, cover 55/270, mid-off 12/320, mid-on −12/320, midwicket −60/270, square leg −95/250, fine leg −160/(b − 30), third man 155/(b − 30).\n1143\t- **Defensive:** point 95/250, deep cover 55/(b − 30), long-off 12/(b − 30), long-on −12/(b − 30), deep midwicket −60/(b − 30), deep square −95/(b − 30), fine leg −160/(b − 30), third man 155/(b − 30), cover 40/260.\n1144\t- **Spin attack:** slip 160/40, short leg −100/50, silly point 100/50, cover 55/240, mid-off 12/280, mid-on −12/280, midwicket −60/240, deep square −95/(b − 30), long-on −15/(b − 30). The keeper stands up at 24.\n1145\t\n1146\t### 8.5 Shots (resolver rows; sectors in batter-frame degrees, + off side, 0 straight, ±180 behind)\n1147\t| Button | Length | Sector | Shot | contactAt | Launch | Speed (u/s) | Zone line / z |\n1148\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1149\t| ✕ | full | −25..25 | straight drive | 0.13 | 3° | 440 | −6..8 / 0..14 |\n1150\t| ✕ | full | 25..75 | cover drive | 0.13 | 4° | 450 | −4..14 / 0..14 |\n1151\t| ✕ | full | −75..−25 | on drive | 0.13 | 4° | 430 | −8..6 / 0..14 |\n1152\t| ✕ | full/good | −130..−75 | flick off the pads | 0.12 | 6° | 400 | −10..2 / 0..18 |\n1153\t| ✕ | full/good | −180..−130 | leg glance | 0.11 | 3° | 330 | −10..0 / 0..20 |\n1154\t| ✕ | good | 25..75 | back-foot punch | 0.12 | 5° | 410 | −4..14 / 6..22 |\n1155\t| ✕ | short | −130..−60 | pull | 0.12 | 8° | 460 | −6..10 / 14..32 |\n1156\t| ✕ | short/good (line > 8 off) | 75..125 | square cut | 0.11 | 5° | 460 | 6..22 / 6..26 |\n1157\t| ✕ | any | 125..180 | late cut / dab | 0.10 | 2° | 300 | 4..20 / 2..22 |\n1158\t| ✕ | any | other | push (in that direction) | 0.12 | 3° | 320 | −8..12 / 0..24 |\n1159\t| □ | full | −30..30 | lofted straight hit | 0.14 | 38° | 330 | −6..8 / 0..16 |\n1160\t| □ | full | 30..80 | inside-out lofted cover | 0.14 | 34° | 320 | −2..16 / 0..16 |\n1161\t| □ | full/good | −110..−30 | slog / slog-sweep (vs spin) | 0.15 | 36° | 335 | −10..8 / 0..20 |\n1162\t| □ | short | −140..−60 | hook | 0.12 | 30° | 340 | −6..10 / 18..38 |\n1163\t| □ | short | 60..120 | upper cut | 0.11 | 34° | 310 | 4..20 / 18..36 |\n1164\t| □ | any | 150..180 or −180..−150 | scoop / ramp (over the keeper) | 0.12 | 42° | 260 | −4..6 / 0..20 |\n1165\t| □ | yorker | −30..30 | helicopter (360° follow-through) | 0.12 | 40° | 350 | −4..6 / 0..6 |\n1166\t| ○ | full/good | any | forward defence | 0.08 | 0° | 60 | −8..12 / 0..20 |\n1167\t| ○ | short | any | back defence (duck if z > 28) | 0.08 | 0° | 50 | −8..12 / 8..28 |\n1168\t| none | — | — | leave (duck or sway if z > 28) | — | — | — | — |\n1169\t\n1170\tLengths are measured from the striker's popping crease to where the ball pitched (or would pitch): yorker ≤ 24, full 24–70, good 70–130, short > 130.\n1171\t\n1172\t### 8.6 Specials\n1173\t| Special | Owner | Kind | Effect |\n1174\t|---|---|---|---|\n1175\t| Tea-Kettle Slog | Edie | bat | guaranteed PERFECT lofted hit in the aimed direction, +25% distance, a steam-whistle trail; any delivery |\n1176\t| Vicar's Revenge | Edie | bowl | a 155 km/h inswinging yorker, green meter, holy-light trail; the edge zone ×1.5 vs the batter |\n1177\t| The Grandad | Basil | bowl | a leg-break that bounces three times (each bounce turns +6°) and still reaches the stumps at a crawl; the batter's timing windows halved (the shock) |\n1178\t| Statistical Certainty | Dev | bat | shows the exact perfect timing marker (a ring closing on the bat) for 1 ball; GOOD guaranteed, PERFECT if pressed on the marker |\n1179\t| The Chirp | Pip | field | while bowling: the next ball halves the CPU batter's timing σ tolerance (it gets flustered), or a human opponent's windows (−30%); costs 50 Hype |\n1180\t| The Long Handle | Gaz (CPU) | bat | a lofted hit with power ×1.4 |\n1181\t| Dibbly-Dobbly Doom | Big Terry (CPU) | bowl | an 80 km/h ball that wobbles in the air; batters mistime it (AI σ ×2) |\n1182\t| Peregrine Swoop | Peregrine | bowl | banana swing ×3, late |\n1183\t| Silver Tray Save | Fortescue | field | the next catch chance is guaranteed (a tray flourish) |\n1184\t| The Croquet Drive | Araminta | bat | a ground shot that can't be stopped (it passes through fielders) and goes for FOUR |\n1185\t| Sunburn Bouncer | Shazza | bowl | a 152 km/h bouncer with heat haze; ducking makes it a dot, a hook without PERFECT gives a top-edge catch |\n1186\t| Boardwalk Bludgeon | Kev | bat | a huge hit, +40% distance, but caught if a fielder is under it |\n1187\t| Vanishing Ball | Spinaldo | bowl | invisible from 40% to 65% of the flight (smoke puffs); the shadow is still drawn (fair) |\n1188\t| Sawn in Half | Zsa-Zsa | bowl | a googly; a bowled wicket splits the stumps |\n1189\t| Lightning Stumping | Houdini Jnr | field | the stumping window triples for 1 over |\n1190\t| Grudge Ball | Thrumpton | bowl | an LBW-seeking yorker; the umpire's accuracy +10% on that ball (a running joke: it doesn't help him) |\n1191\t| Grudge Drive | Thrumpton | bat | a power drive straight at the bowler |\n1192\t| Triple Threat | Thrumptonator | bowl | releases 3 balls: 2 holograms on different lines and lengths, 1 real one (with a seam glint every 0.1 s); only the real one matters |\n1193\t| Ectoplasmic Edge | Grimble | bat | the ball passes through the first fielder it meets |\n1194\t\n1195\t### 8.7 Items, tea treats and chaos\n1196\t#### 8.7.1 Items (Kerfuffle rules)\n1197\t| Item | Side | Effect |\n1198\t|---|---|---|\n1199\t| Golden Teapot | bat | the next scoring shot's runs ×2 (the bonus is shown) |\n1200\t| Lucky Horseshoe | bat | the next dismissal is overturned (\"The ball hits the horseshoe! NOT OUT!\") |\n1201\t| Giant Bat | bat | the bat is drawn 1.6× bigger; zones and windows ×1.4 for 2 balls |\n1202\t| Cake Slice | bat or bowl | Hype +40 |\n1203\t| Sticky Gloves | bowl | the next catch chance is guaranteed |\n1204\t| Banana Peel | bowl | the next run attempt: batters slip mid-pitch (−40% speed for 1 s) |\n1205\t| Fog Machine | bowl | the next ball: the batter's pitch marker is hidden; CPU σ ×1.5 |\n1206\t\n1207\t**Tea treats** (story, at the innings break, pick one): Victoria Sponge (Hype +40), Builder's Tea (timing windows +10% for 2 overs), Cucumber Sandwiches (run speed +10% for the innings).\n1208\t\n1209\t#### 8.7.2 Stadium targets\n1210\tSee §8.3. Each is an entry `{ id, ground, shape: 'box'|'sphere', at, size, bonus, hype: 30, state, fx, line }`.\n1211\t\n1212\t#### 8.7.3 Chaos events\n1213\tEach event is `{ id, ground, when: 'between'|'overStart', chance, duration, run(game, match) generator }`. Each must end by itself and restore the field:\n1214\t- Doris the cow: walks the outfield on a path; fielders path round her; she leaves after 2 overs, or at once if a ball hits her, harmlessly (\"She's taken it on the flank and seems pleased\");\n1215\t- bees from the hive: chase a fielder (−30% speed) for 1 over;\n1216\t- church bells: cosmetic, plus a commentary line;\n1217\t- peacocks: wander and deflect ground balls ±25°;\n1218\t- Fortescue's tea tray: a fielder runs on with tea; play pauses 3 s;\n1219\t- seagulls: a stopped ball in the outfield is carried 30 units (2 byes);\n1220\t- the tide: the sea-side boundary is re-baked between overs. The floor bake is a known cost: mark the tide as a \"between-overs re-bake\" and draw the water edge as an animated overlay band, so only one bake per over happens;\n1221\t- the rain delay (scripted in chapter 4; available in Quick Match weather \"rain\"): rain, covers, tea scene, the Kerfuffle Method;\n1222\t- dust devils: deflect aerial balls passing through ±10°;\n1223\t- rabbits: cosmetic;\n1224\t- fog banks: change the fog density over 2 overs;\n1225\t- ghost phasing: a ghost fielder is intangible for 0.5 s at random;\n1226\t- fireworks: on sixes at night;\n1227\t- the advert break: a 3 s card between overs at the Megadome;\n1228\t- the mascot pitch invader: a chicken costume, chased by stewards; cosmetic, 1 over, any ground in Quick Match with Kerfuffle rules.\n1229\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"10fd43c2-a819-4540-9aa0-cc285e3b03f8","uuid":"b3eb9786-ffaa-4441-a7d0-31e1d55012cf","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:34:20.139Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174825__x17a627/work/PLAN.md","content":"| yorker | pace | 136–146 | 0.15 | 0.5 | 0 | 0.9 | 0.1 | length band 0–24 from the crease |\n| slower | pace | 105–115 | 0 | 1.2 | 0 | 0.95 | 0.3 | looks like an express until late (no speed shown until it pitches) |\n| outswing | swing | 125–135 | +1.0 | 1.0 | 0 | 1.0 | 0 | |\n| inswing | swing | 125–135 | −1.0 | 1.0 | 0 | 1.0 | 0 | |\n| wobble | swing | 120–130 | ±0.3 random | 3.0 | 0 | 1.0 | 0 | |\n| dobber | medium | 100–110 | 0.1 | 1.5 | 0 | 0.95 | 0.1 | |\n| cutter | medium | 105–115 | 0 | 1.0 | +3 | 0.95 | 0 | |\n| knuckle | medium | 95–105 | wobbly flight | 0.5 | 0 | 0.9 | 0.25 | |\n| legbreak | spin | 78–88 | drift −0.3 | 0.3 | +9 | 1.05 | 0.2 | |\n| googly | spin | 76–86 | drift +0.2 | 0.3 | −8 | 1.05 | 0.2 | |\n| topspin | spin | 80–90 | 0 | 0.3 | 0 | 1.2 | 0.35 | |\n| offbreak | spin | 80–90 | drift +0.3 | 0.3 | −8 | 1.0 | 0.15 | |\n| armball | spin | 88–96 | +0.3 | 0.3 | 0 | 0.95 | 0 | |\n| doosra | spin | 78–88 | 0 | 0.3 | +8 | 1.05 | 0.2 | |\n| piston | machine | 160–170 | 0 | 0.8 | 0 | 1.05 | 0 | the Thrumptonator only |\n| steamBouncer | machine | 150 | 0 | 1.0 | 0 | 1.35 | 0 | steam trail |\n| spinCycle | machine | 95 | 0 | 0 | ±14 random | 1.1 | 0.3 | |\n\nSwing base acceleration: 60 u/s² × swing × `T('swing')` × ground factor. Each bowler lists 3 deliveries from their family (plus a special).\n\n#### 8.4.2 Field presets (θ° from straight, + = off side; distance in units; the keeper is extra)\n- **Attacking pace:** slip1 165/150, slip2 158/150, slip3 151/152, gully 132/150, point 95/230, cover 58/260, mid-off 14/300, mid-on −14/300, fine leg −162/(boundary − 30).\n- **Balanced:** slip1 165/150, point 95/240, cover 55/270, mid-off 12/320, mid-on −12/320, midwicket −60/270, square leg −95/250, fine leg −160/(b − 30), third man 155/(b − 30).\n- **Defensive:** point 95/250, deep cover 55/(b − 30), long-off 12/(b − 30), long-on −12/(b − 30), deep midwicket −60/(b − 30), deep square −95/(b − 30), fine leg −160/(b − 30), third man 155/(b − 30), cover 40/260.\n- **Spin attack:** slip 160/40, short leg −100/50, silly point 100/50, cover 55/240, mid-off 12/280, mid-on −12/280, midwicket −60/240, deep square −95/(b − 30), long-on −15/(b − 30). The keeper stands up at 24.\n\n### 8.5 Shots (resolver rows; sectors in batter-frame degrees, + off side, 0 straight, ±180 behind)\n| Button | Length | Sector | Shot | contactAt | Launch | Speed (u/s) | Zone line / z |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| ✕ | full | −25..25 | straight drive | 0.13 | 3° | 440 | −6..8 / 0..14 |\n| ✕ | full | 25..75 | cover drive | 0.13 | 4° | 450 | −4..14 / 0..14 |\n| ✕ | full | −75..−25 | on drive | 0.13 | 4° | 430 | −8..6 / 0..14 |\n| ✕ | full/good | −130..−75 | flick off the pads | 0.12 | 6° | 400 | −10..2 / 0..18 |\n| ✕ | full/good | −180..−130 | leg glance | 0.11 | 3° | 330 | −10..0 / 0..20 |\n| ✕ | good | 25..75 | back-foot punch | 0.12 | 5° | 410 | −4..14 / 6..22 |\n| ✕ | short | −130..−60 | pull | 0.12 | 8° | 460 | −6..10 / 14..32 |\n| ✕ | short/good (line > 8 off) | 75..125 | square cut | 0.11 | 5° | 460 | 6..22 / 6..26 |\n| ✕ | any | 125..180 | late cut / dab | 0.10 | 2° | 300 | 4..20 / 2..22 |\n| ✕ | any | other | push (in that direction) | 0.12 | 3° | 320 | −8..12 / 0..24 |\n| □ | full | −30..30 | lofted straight hit | 0.14 | 38° | 330 | −6..8 / 0..16 |\n| □ | full | 30..80 | inside-out lofted cover | 0.14 | 34° | 320 | −2..16 / 0..16 |\n| □ | full/good | −110..−30 | slog / slog-sweep (vs spin) | 0.15 | 36° | 335 | −10..8 / 0..20 |\n| □ | short | −140..−60 | hook | 0.12 | 30° | 340 | −6..10 / 18..38 |\n| □ | short | 60..120 | upper cut | 0.11 | 34° | 310 | 4..20 / 18..36 |\n| □ | any | 150..180 or −180..−150 | scoop / ramp (over the keeper) | 0.12 | 42° | 260 | −4..6 / 0..20 |\n| □ | yorker | −30..30 | helicopter (360° follow-through) | 0.12 | 40° | 350 | −4..6 / 0..6 |\n| ○ | full/good | any | forward defence | 0.08 | 0° | 60 | −8..12 / 0..20 |\n| ○ | short | any | back defence (duck if z > 28) | 0.08 | 0° | 50 | −8..12 / 8..28 |\n| none | — | — | leave (duck or sway if z > 28) | — | — | — | — |\n\nLengths are measured from the striker's popping crease to where the ball pitched (or would pitch): yorker ≤ 24, full 24–70, good 70–130, short > 130.\n\n### 8.6 Specials\n| Special | Owner | Kind | Effect |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Tea-Kettle Slog | Edie | bat | guaranteed PERFECT lofted hit in the aimed direction, +25% distance, a steam-whistle trail; any delivery |\n| Vicar's Revenge | Edie | bowl | a 155 km/h inswinging yorker, green meter, holy-light trail; the edge zone ×1.5 vs the batter |\n| The Grandad | Basil | bowl | a leg-break that bounces three times (each bounce turns +6°) and still reaches the stumps at a crawl; the batter's timing windows halved (the shock) |\n| Statistical Certainty | Dev | bat | shows the exact perfect timing marker (a ring closing on the bat) for 1 ball; GOOD guaranteed, PERFECT if pressed on the marker |\n| The Chirp | Pip | field | while bowling: the next ball halves the CPU batter's timing σ tolerance (it gets flustered), or a human opponent's windows (−30%); costs 50 Hype |\n| The Long Handle | Gaz (CPU) | bat | a lofted hit with power ×1.4 |\n| Dibbly-Dobbly Doom | Big Terry (CPU) | bowl | an 80 km/h ball that wobbles in the air; batters mistime it (AI σ ×2) |\n| Peregrine Swoop | Peregrine | bowl | banana swing ×3, late |\n| Silver Tray Save | Fortescue | field | the next catch chance is guaranteed (a tray flourish) |\n| The Croquet Drive | Araminta | bat | a ground shot that can't be stopped (it passes through fielders) and goes for FOUR |\n| Sunburn Bouncer | Shazza | bowl | a 152 km/h bouncer with heat haze; ducking makes it a dot, a hook without PERFECT gives a top-edge catch |\n| Boardwalk Bludgeon | Kev | bat | a huge hit, +40% distance, but caught if a fielder is under it |\n| Vanishing Ball | Spinaldo | bowl | invisible from 40% to 65% of the flight (smoke puffs); the shadow is still drawn (fair) |\n| Sawn in Half | Zsa-Zsa | bowl | a googly; a bowled wicket splits the stumps |\n| Lightning Stumping | Houdini Jnr | field | the stumping window triples for 1 over |\n| Grudge Ball | Thrumpton | bowl | an LBW-seeking yorker; the umpire's accuracy +10% on that ball (a running joke: it doesn't help him) |\n| Grudge Drive | Thrumpton | bat | a power drive straight at the bowler |\n| Triple Threat | Thrumptonator | bowl | releases 3 balls: 2 holograms on different lines and lengths, 1 real one (with a seam glint every 0.1 s); only the real one matters |\n| Ectoplasmic Edge | Grimble | bat | the ball passes through the first fielder it meets |\n\n### 8.7 Items, tea treats and chaos\n#### 8.7.1 Items (Kerfuffle rules)\n| Item | Side | Effect |\n|---|---|---|\n| Golden Teapot | bat | the next scoring shot's runs ×2 (the bonus is shown) |\n| Lucky Horseshoe | bat | the next dismissal is overturned (\"The ball hits the horseshoe! NOT OUT!\") |\n| Giant Bat | bat | the bat is drawn 1.6× bigger; zones and windows ×1.4 for 2 balls |\n| Cake Slice | bat or bowl | Hype +40 |\n| Sticky Gloves | bowl | the next catch chance is guaranteed |\n| Banana Peel | bowl | the next run attempt: batters slip mid-pitch (−40% speed for 1 s) |\n| Fog Machine | bowl | the next ball: the batter's pitch marker is hidden; CPU σ ×1.5 |\n\n**Tea treats** (story, at the innings break, pick one): Victoria Sponge (Hype +40), Builder's Tea (timing windows +10% for 2 overs), Cucumber Sandwiches (run speed +10% for the innings).\n\n#### 8.7.2 Stadium targets\nSee §8.3. Each is an entry `{ id, ground, shape: 'box'|'sphere', at, size, bonus, hype: 30, state, fx, line }`.\n\n#### 8.7.3 Chaos events\nEach event is `{ id, ground, when: 'between'|'overStart', chance, duration, run(game, match) generator }`. Each must end by itself and restore the field:\n- Doris the cow: walks the outfield on a path; fielders path round her; she leaves after 2 overs, or at once if a ball hits her, harmlessly (\"She's taken it on the flank and seems pleased\");\n- bees from the hive: chase a fielder (−30% speed) for 1 over;\n- church bells: cosmetic, plus a commentary line;\n- peacocks: wander and deflect ground balls ±25°;\n- Fortescue's tea tray: a fielder runs on with tea; play pauses 3 s;\n- seagulls: a stopped ball in the outfield is carried 30 units (2 byes);\n- the tide: the sea-side boundary is re-baked between overs. The floor bake is a known cost: mark the tide as a \"between-overs re-bake\" and draw the water edge as an animated overlay band, so only one bake per over happens;\n- the rain delay (scripted in chapter 4; available in Quick Match weather \"rain\"): rain, covers, tea scene, the Kerfuffle Method;\n- dust devils: deflect aerial balls passing through ±10°;\n- rabbits: cosmetic;\n- fog banks: change the fog density over 2 overs;\n- ghost phasing: a ghost fielder is intangible for 0.5 s at random;\n- fireworks: on sixes at night;\n- the advert break: a 3 s card between overs at the Megadome;\n- the mascot pitch invader: a chicken costume, chased by stewards; cosmetic, 1 over, any ground in Quick Match with Kerfuffle rules.\n","numLines":110,"startLine":1120,"totalLines":1435}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0149Fn6tve4FmNJuHbajSPps","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
