{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HnzDWW5EtGHPkQfwTcaKRi","type":"tool_result","content":"1333\t## 11. Testing\n1334\t\n1335\t### 11.1 The one command\n1336\t`node test/run.mjs [suite ...]`, run from `<dev>`:\n1337\t- it runs every suite, or only those named;\n1338\t- it prints **only failures**, as `FAIL <suite> › <case>: <detail>`;\n1339\t- then one line: `142 passed, 0 failed (14 suites, 63.4 s)`;\n1340\t- the exit code is 1 on any failure.\n1341\t\n1342\tBrowser suites need `cd engine && npm install && npx playwright install chromium` once. If Playwright is missing, the runner prints that as a failure; it never skips silently.\n1343\t\n1344\tRerun only the suites covering the code you changed (`node test/run.mjs unit-ball sim-batting`).\n1345\t\n1346\t### 11.2 How the game is driven headless\n1347\t- Load `engine/my-3d2dge.js` and `dist/game.js` into a `vm` context with the stand-ins `window`, `addEventListener`, `location` and `matchMedia` (as `engine/kits/test.mjs` does), then `game = E.current`.\n1348\t- Drive with `game.advance(seconds)` (exact 1/120 s steps), `game.input.tap/hold/press/release`, and `input.feed` for the mouse. Seed `Math.random = E.rng(7)` and `MatchConfig.seed`.\n1349\t- `game.debug` (80-debug.js) provides:\n1350\t  - `snapshot()`: `{ scene, mode, ui: { device, glyphs, touchGate, prompts: [...], menuFocus }, match: { innings, runs, wkts, balls, over, target, need, freeHit, striker, nonStriker, bowler, hype: [a, b], fire, items, result }, ball: { phase, x, y, z, v, pitched, fx }, last (the last ball record), director: { state, shot }, story: { chapter, beat, flags }, attract: { active, segment }, hub: { active, phase, sent: { progress, result } }, dev: { open, changed: [...] }, coverage: {...}, errors }`;\n1351\t  - `idealPress()`: the step to press for a PERFECT on the current ball;\n1352\t  - `forceDelivery(spec)`, `forceOutcome(kind)`, `startMatch(cfg)`, `startChapter(n, beat)`, `setTuning(k, v)`, `spawnItem(id, at)`, `triggerChaos(id)`, `skipTo(state)`.\n1353\t- **The coverage tracker** marks features as they happen (each delivery family, shot family, dismissal, special, item, target, chaos event, camera shot, review, rain, fog, night, Super Over, mix-up, dive, overthrow). Bot and attract suites assert on it.\n1354\t\n1355\t### 11.3 Suites\n1356\t| Suite | What it checks |\n1357\t|---|---|\n1358\t| `unit-ball` | §5.1 tests |\n1359\t| `unit-rules` | §5.7.6 |\n1360\t| `unit-shots` | §5.3: resolver rows, timing grades, edges |\n1361\t| `unit-umpire` | §5.6 |\n1362\t| `unit-ui` | HUD layout overlap on 4 sizes; the glyph mapping for codes; line lengths after the template fill (§5.12); hub tag lengths |\n1363\t| `sim-batting` | ~12 scenarios (§5.3 tests), driven by real input at `idealPress() ± offsets` |\n1364\t| `sim-bowling` | ~8 scenarios (§5.2) |\n1365\t| `sim-running-fielding` | ~12 scenarios (§5.4, §5.5) |\n1366\t| `sim-arcade` | every special, item, target and chaos event forced once: its effect observable, no errors, the state restored afterwards |\n1367\t| `sim-front` | title → menu by keys, pad and mouse (hover and click); settings items exist; the pause menu has our items; dev mode open, slider change, reset; the About pages hold every Source Information field and the 3 feedback lists; the touch-only gate; prompts follow the device; Xbox glyph setting |\n1368\t| `sim-mp` | local players join; roles; co-op agreement and mix-up; per-player prompts |\n1369\t| `bot-match` | CPU vs CPU, 2 overs, on each of the 5 grounds and the 3 times of day. Each must finish with a result. Totals must be plausible (runs 5–90 per innings, extras < 30%). No director state may exceed its timeout, and every ball must end within 15 s. There must be no errors, and the coverage must include ≥ 1 four, ≥ 1 wicket and ≥ 1 run. |\n1370\t| `bot-campaign` | New Game → prologue → chapters 1–5 → ending → credits, all by virtual input from the autopilot. The autopilot uses the AI's judgment (no cheats) at Village difficulty, with up to 3 retries per chapter. All beats must fire in order, all goals be evaluated, the save show complete and Continue work after a reload. It also asserts the duration and that there are no errors. |\n1371\t| `attract-coverage` | §5.18 |\n1372\t| `dev` | §5.19.3 |\n1373\t| `hub-mock` | §5.17.3 |\n1374\t| `bundle` | the file name; the session client is the first script after the charset meta, identical to vendor; hub and catalogue tags are present and valid; no external URLs in `src=` or `fetch(`; no `TODO`, `FIXME` or `placeholder` in `src/`; `exit-interview.json` (when present) parses and every value is non-empty |\n1375\t| `browser-smoke` | Playwright via `engine/tools/check.mjs` on the bundle and deep links (`#match`, `#nets`, `#about`, `#dev`; implement hash deep links in `99-start.js` for tools only): no errors or engine warnings; its look notes printed as failures only if they're severe (low contrast or flat areas on the match scene). Screenshots are saved to `test/out/` |\n1376\t| `browser-hub` | §5.17.3 harness runs |\n1377\t\n1378\t### 11.4 Balance tests (run in M7; they report, not gate)\n1379\t`node test/balance.mjs` runs 200 CPU-vs-CPU balls per difficulty and per ground, and prints the run rate, wickets per over, boundary share and extras share. Targets at County: about 8–11 runs an over, about 0.6 wickets an over, extras below 10%. Tune with the dev sliders, then copy the values into the defaults.\n1380\t\n1381\t### 11.5 Screenshots and filmstrips (what scripts can't check)\n1382\tReview with your own eyes, saved under `test/out/`:\n1383\t- the title;\n1384\t- each ground in broadcast and wide (10 shots) at 427×240, plus one at 320×690 and one at 640×270;\n1385\t- each team kit (6);\n1386\t- the HUD in batting, bowling and fielding;\n1387\t- the third-umpire screen, Owl-Eye, an ON FIRE batter, each special's FX (still frames);\n1388\t- the story map, a cutscene with portraits, the results screen with its report;\n1389\t- the dev panel (legible at 10 feet: view at 1920×1080 scaled to 25%);\n1390\t- the touch-only gate and each About page;\n1391\t- filmstrips: 6 shot families, the pace and spin bowling actions, the dive, the diving catch, umpire signals OUT, FOUR and SIX.\n1392\t\n1393\t---\n1394\t\n1395\t## 12. Final delivery checklist\n1396\t- [ ] `CricketKerfuffle-Cricket-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174825.html` in the root: one file, opens from file:// to the title, no network requests, and the AI Hub client is the first script in `<head>`.\n1397\t- [ ] Every feature in §5 is present and reachable in play: no TODOs, placeholders or stubs.\n1398\t- [ ] Attract mode after 10 s idle on the title and menus; any input exits.\n1399\t- [ ] Dev mode from the pause menu: live sliders with reset to defaults, toggles and jumps.\n1400\t- [ ] AI Hub: the harness passes for 1, 2 and 4 players, and the game runs standalone outside a session.\n1401\t- [ ] Controller-first 10-foot UI; keyboard and mouse native; prompts follow the last device; PlayStation glyphs, with Xbox in Settings; the touch-only gate.\n1402\t- [ ] All audio in code, with gibberish voices.\n1403\t- [ ] `node test/run.mjs` prints `… passed, 0 failed`.\n1404\t- [ ] The About/Credits pages and the **chat reply** both carry Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback, with \"unknown\" where unconfirmed.\n1405\t- [ ] `exit-interview.json` in the root: the exact shape from TASK.md, parses as JSON, every value filled.\n1406\t- [ ] `engine/CHANGES-KERFUFFLE.md` lists the engine changes, and the Engine Feedback answers name them.\n1407\t- [ ] All processes you started are stopped by PID.\n1408\t\n1409\t---\n1410\t\n1411\t## 13. Where each TASK.md requirement is met\n1412\t| TASK.md requirement | Plan |\n1413\t|---|---|\n1414\t| Genre and perspective chosen to fit cricket (over-the-top arcade) | §2, §5.11 |\n1415\t| Title: a riff on the name, 50 brainstormed, picked by a real RNG | header |\n1416\t| Single HTML file, named as given | §1.1, §3.6 |\n1417\t| Build on the my-3d2dge handoff; free to change the engine | §1.2, §3.1, §3.5 |\n1418\t| Engine's native style plus new source-specific art | §6 |\n1419\t| Engine's native animation plus new animations | §7 |\n1420\t| All audio in code, with gibberish voices | §5.13 |\n1421\t| Online: AI Hub lib/hub, and the game on its own | §5.17, §5.16.5 |\n1422\t| Dev subfolder and bundling; file:// preferred; servers on port 0; PID-only stops | §1.2, §3.2, §3.6, §11 |\n1423\t| Performance budget unlimited | §1.3, §6 |\n1424\t| Headless testing with game.advance and game.debug, a scripted full playthrough, one command with failures and a count | §11 |\n1425\t| A feature-complete vertical slice that captures the source's world, characters, themes and tone | §2, §8 |\n1426\t| Dev mode from pause, live sliders and reset | §5.19 |\n1427\t| Attract mode after 10 s idle; any input exits; AI may cheat | §5.18 |\n1428\t| Multiplayer | §5.16.5, §5.17 |\n1429\t| Narrative tone like the source's | §5.12, §8.8, §8.9 |\n1430\t| 10-foot controller-first UI; native keyboard and mouse; hover focus; device-following prompts; PS glyphs with an Xbox option; no dense data screens | §5.14, §5.15 |\n1431\t| Touch-only: no touch controls, \"Controller or keyboard required\", the settings button, attract runs | §5.15.6 |\n1432\t| No TODOs, placeholders or stubs | §1.3, §11.3 (the bundle grep), §12 |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"10fd43c2-a819-4540-9aa0-cc285e3b03f8","uuid":"ed1a661e-d3c1-4f74-a707-7dbcac274860","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:35:05.844Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174825__x17a627/work/PLAN.md","content":"## 11. Testing\n\n### 11.1 The one command\n`node test/run.mjs [suite ...]`, run from `<dev>`:\n- it runs every suite, or only those named;\n- it prints **only failures**, as `FAIL <suite> › <case>: <detail>`;\n- then one line: `142 passed, 0 failed (14 suites, 63.4 s)`;\n- the exit code is 1 on any failure.\n\nBrowser suites need `cd engine && npm install && npx playwright install chromium` once. If Playwright is missing, the runner prints that as a failure; it never skips silently.\n\nRerun only the suites covering the code you changed (`node test/run.mjs unit-ball sim-batting`).\n\n### 11.2 How the game is driven headless\n- Load `engine/my-3d2dge.js` and `dist/game.js` into a `vm` context with the stand-ins `window`, `addEventListener`, `location` and `matchMedia` (as `engine/kits/test.mjs` does), then `game = E.current`.\n- Drive with `game.advance(seconds)` (exact 1/120 s steps), `game.input.tap/hold/press/release`, and `input.feed` for the mouse. Seed `Math.random = E.rng(7)` and `MatchConfig.seed`.\n- `game.debug` (80-debug.js) provides:\n  - `snapshot()`: `{ scene, mode, ui: { device, glyphs, touchGate, prompts: [...], menuFocus }, match: { innings, runs, wkts, balls, over, target, need, freeHit, striker, nonStriker, bowler, hype: [a, b], fire, items, result }, ball: { phase, x, y, z, v, pitched, fx }, last (the last ball record), director: { state, shot }, story: { chapter, beat, flags }, attract: { active, segment }, hub: { active, phase, sent: { progress, result } }, dev: { open, changed: [...] }, coverage: {...}, errors }`;\n  - `idealPress()`: the step to press for a PERFECT on the current ball;\n  - `forceDelivery(spec)`, `forceOutcome(kind)`, `startMatch(cfg)`, `startChapter(n, beat)`, `setTuning(k, v)`, `spawnItem(id, at)`, `triggerChaos(id)`, `skipTo(state)`.\n- **The coverage tracker** marks features as they happen (each delivery family, shot family, dismissal, special, item, target, chaos event, camera shot, review, rain, fog, night, Super Over, mix-up, dive, overthrow). Bot and attract suites assert on it.\n\n### 11.3 Suites\n| Suite | What it checks |\n|---|---|\n| `unit-ball` | §5.1 tests |\n| `unit-rules` | §5.7.6 |\n| `unit-shots` | §5.3: resolver rows, timing grades, edges |\n| `unit-umpire` | §5.6 |\n| `unit-ui` | HUD layout overlap on 4 sizes; the glyph mapping for codes; line lengths after the template fill (§5.12); hub tag lengths |\n| `sim-batting` | ~12 scenarios (§5.3 tests), driven by real input at `idealPress() ± offsets` |\n| `sim-bowling` | ~8 scenarios (§5.2) |\n| `sim-running-fielding` | ~12 scenarios (§5.4, §5.5) |\n| `sim-arcade` | every special, item, target and chaos event forced once: its effect observable, no errors, the state restored afterwards |\n| `sim-front` | title → menu by keys, pad and mouse (hover and click); settings items exist; the pause menu has our items; dev mode open, slider change, reset; the About pages hold every Source Information field and the 3 feedback lists; the touch-only gate; prompts follow the device; Xbox glyph setting |\n| `sim-mp` | local players join; roles; co-op agreement and mix-up; per-player prompts |\n| `bot-match` | CPU vs CPU, 2 overs, on each of the 5 grounds and the 3 times of day. Each must finish with a result. Totals must be plausible (runs 5–90 per innings, extras < 30%). No director state may exceed its timeout, and every ball must end within 15 s. There must be no errors, and the coverage must include ≥ 1 four, ≥ 1 wicket and ≥ 1 run. |\n| `bot-campaign` | New Game → prologue → chapters 1–5 → ending → credits, all by virtual input from the autopilot. The autopilot uses the AI's judgment (no cheats) at Village difficulty, with up to 3 retries per chapter. All beats must fire in order, all goals be evaluated, the save show complete and Continue work after a reload. It also asserts the duration and that there are no errors. |\n| `attract-coverage` | §5.18 |\n| `dev` | §5.19.3 |\n| `hub-mock` | §5.17.3 |\n| `bundle` | the file name; the session client is the first script after the charset meta, identical to vendor; hub and catalogue tags are present and valid; no external URLs in `src=` or `fetch(`; no `TODO`, `FIXME` or `placeholder` in `src/`; `exit-interview.json` (when present) parses and every value is non-empty |\n| `browser-smoke` | Playwright via `engine/tools/check.mjs` on the bundle and deep links (`#match`, `#nets`, `#about`, `#dev`; implement hash deep links in `99-start.js` for tools only): no errors or engine warnings; its look notes printed as failures only if they're severe (low contrast or flat areas on the match scene). Screenshots are saved to `test/out/` |\n| `browser-hub` | §5.17.3 harness runs |\n\n### 11.4 Balance tests (run in M7; they report, not gate)\n`node test/balance.mjs` runs 200 CPU-vs-CPU balls per difficulty and per ground, and prints the run rate, wickets per over, boundary share and extras share. Targets at County: about 8–11 runs an over, about 0.6 wickets an over, extras below 10%. Tune with the dev sliders, then copy the values into the defaults.\n\n### 11.5 Screenshots and filmstrips (what scripts can't check)\nReview with your own eyes, saved under `test/out/`:\n- the title;\n- each ground in broadcast and wide (10 shots) at 427×240, plus one at 320×690 and one at 640×270;\n- each team kit (6);\n- the HUD in batting, bowling and fielding;\n- the third-umpire screen, Owl-Eye, an ON FIRE batter, each special's FX (still frames);\n- the story map, a cutscene with portraits, the results screen with its report;\n- the dev panel (legible at 10 feet: view at 1920×1080 scaled to 25%);\n- the touch-only gate and each About page;\n- filmstrips: 6 shot families, the pace and spin bowling actions, the dive, the diving catch, umpire signals OUT, FOUR and SIX.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Final delivery checklist\n- [ ] `CricketKerfuffle-Cricket-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174825.html` in the root: one file, opens from file:// to the title, no network requests, and the AI Hub client is the first script in `<head>`.\n- [ ] Every feature in §5 is present and reachable in play: no TODOs, placeholders or stubs.\n- [ ] Attract mode after 10 s idle on the title and menus; any input exits.\n- [ ] Dev mode from the pause menu: live sliders with reset to defaults, toggles and jumps.\n- [ ] AI Hub: the harness passes for 1, 2 and 4 players, and the game runs standalone outside a session.\n- [ ] Controller-first 10-foot UI; keyboard and mouse native; prompts follow the last device; PlayStation glyphs, with Xbox in Settings; the touch-only gate.\n- [ ] All audio in code, with gibberish voices.\n- [ ] `node test/run.mjs` prints `… passed, 0 failed`.\n- [ ] The About/Credits pages and the **chat reply** both carry Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback, with \"unknown\" where unconfirmed.\n- [ ] `exit-interview.json` in the root: the exact shape from TASK.md, parses as JSON, every value filled.\n- [ ] `engine/CHANGES-KERFUFFLE.md` lists the engine changes, and the Engine Feedback answers name them.\n- [ ] All processes you started are stopped by PID.\n\n---\n\n## 13. Where each TASK.md requirement is met\n| TASK.md requirement | Plan |\n|---|---|\n| Genre and perspective chosen to fit cricket (over-the-top arcade) | §2, §5.11 |\n| Title: a riff on the name, 50 brainstormed, picked by a real RNG | header |\n| Single HTML file, named as given | §1.1, §3.6 |\n| Build on the my-3d2dge handoff; free to change the engine | §1.2, §3.1, §3.5 |\n| Engine's native style plus new source-specific art | §6 |\n| Engine's native animation plus new animations | §7 |\n| All audio in code, with gibberish voices | §5.13 |\n| Online: AI Hub lib/hub, and the game on its own | §5.17, §5.16.5 |\n| Dev subfolder and bundling; file:// preferred; servers on port 0; PID-only stops | §1.2, §3.2, §3.6, §11 |\n| Performance budget unlimited | §1.3, §6 |\n| Headless testing with game.advance and game.debug, a scripted full playthrough, one command with failures and a count | §11 |\n| A feature-complete vertical slice that captures the source's world, characters, themes and tone | §2, §8 |\n| Dev mode from pause, live sliders and reset | §5.19 |\n| Attract mode after 10 s idle; any input exits; AI may cheat | §5.18 |\n| Multiplayer | §5.16.5, §5.17 |\n| Narrative tone like the source's | §5.12, §8.8, §8.9 |\n| 10-foot controller-first UI; native keyboard and mouse; hover focus; device-following prompts; PS glyphs with an Xbox option; no dense data screens | §5.14, §5.15 |\n| Touch-only: no touch controls, \"Controller or keyboard required\", the settings button, attract runs | §5.15.6 |\n| No TODOs, placeholders or stubs | §1.3, §11.3 (the bundle grep), §12 |","numLines":100,"startLine":1333,"totalLines":1435}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01HnzDWW5EtGHPkQfwTcaKRi","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
